{"reason": "TabularResNet currently plateaus at 0.7849 validation accuracy and overfits prematurely as training loss drops to 0.3192 while validation loss diverges to 0.4842. The root cause is the absence of conditional routing: Spaceship Titanic tabular records have strict regime dependencies (such as CryoSleep passengers having zero amenity expenditures), yet the network naively sums continuous and categorical embeddings and uses unconditioned GELU feedforward blocks. Modifying model_design to introduce gated contextual fusion and Gated Linear Unit (GLU) residual blocks directly equips the network with dynamic channel suppression, preventing memorization of noise while preserving representation capacity.", "module": ["model_design"], "plan": {"model_design": "1) WHAT: Upgrade TabularResNet architecture by replacing naive additive feature combination with a Gated Contextual Fusion layer and replacing standard GELU feedforward layers in TabularResNetBlock with Gated Linear Unit (GLU) residual blocks. 2) WHY: In Spaceship Titanic, categorical status such as CryoSleep or CabinDeck strictly modulates the relevance of continuous spending features; standard dense feedforward layers cannot dynamically suppress uninformative channels, leading to cross-modal interference and overfitting. 3) HOW: In TabularResNet, concatenate projected numerical features and categorical embeddings and route them through a learned gating projection before feeding them into the residual backbone; in TabularResNetBlock, implement a GLU layer that projects normalized input into parallel value and gate tensors, computing their element-wise product (Value * sigmoid(Gate)) prior to residual projection and dropout. 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve the TabularResNet and TabularResNetBlock class interfaces and their forward signatures forward(x_num, x_cat) -> logits, maintaining full compatibility with the existing training loop, loss function, and evaluation pipeline."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "TabularResNet currently plateaus at 0.7849 validation accuracy and overfits prematurely as training loss drops to 0.3192 while validation loss diverges to 0.4842. The root cause is the absence of conditional routing: Spaceship Titanic tabular records have strict regime dependencies (such as CryoSleep passengers having zero amenity expenditures), yet the network naively sums continuous and categorical embeddings and uses unconditioned GELU feedforward blocks. Modifying model_design to introduce gated contextual fusion and Gated Linear Unit (GLU) residual blocks directly equips the network with dynamic channel suppression, preventing memorization of noise while preserving representation capacity.",
  "module": [
    "model_design"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "model_design": "1) WHAT: Upgrade TabularResNet architecture by replacing naive additive feature combination with a Gated Contextual Fusion layer and replacing standard GELU feedforward layers in TabularResNetBlock with Gated Linear Unit (GLU) residual blocks. 2) WHY: In Spaceship Titanic, categorical status such as CryoSleep or CabinDeck strictly modulates the relevance of continuous spending features; standard dense feedforward layers cannot dynamically suppress uninformative channels, leading to cross-modal interference and overfitting. 3) HOW: In TabularResNet, concatenate projected numerical features and categorical embeddings and route them through a learned gating projection before feeding them into the residual backbone; in TabularResNetBlock, implement a GLU layer that projects normalized input into parallel value and gate tensors, computing their element-wise product (Value * sigmoid(Gate)) prior to residual projection and dropout. 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve the TabularResNet and TabularResNetBlock class interfaces and their forward signatures forward(x_num, x_cat) -> logits, maintaining full compatibility with the existing training loop, loss function, and evaluation pipeline."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "The baseline model plateaued at 81.35% validation accuracy with high inter-fold variance due to representation bottlenecks: 1D scalar linear tokenization cannot capture zero-inflated luxury expenditure thresholds, discrete boolean predictors such as CryoSleep are diluted by standard scaling, and a single [CLS] token readout bottleneck discards feature activations. Focusing on data_processing_and_feature_engineering and model_design directly resolves these root causes by cleanly isolating discrete switches into categorical embeddings and replacing linear projections with periodic non-linear tokenizers and attentive residual pooling.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Reclassify binary indicators (CryoSleep, VIP, HasSpent, IsSolo, IsSoloFamily, IsInfant, IsChild, IsTeen, IsSenior) and discrete spatial indicators (CabinRegion) from numerical continuous features into categorical features. WHY: CryoSleep is the most decisive predictor in the dataset, and boolean states represent discrete qualitative regimes; standardizing them as continuous floats forces an arbitrary linear scale, whereas categorical assignment allows the model to learn unconstrained distinct embeddings. HOW: In process_features(), append these discrete columns to categorical_cols, ensure non-negative integer encoding without deprecated downcasting warnings, and leave strictly continuous features in numerical_cols. Interface constraints: Retain the function signature process_features() returning (train_processed, test_processed, categorical_cols, numerical_cols) and maintain consistent column names.", "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the 1D linear NumericalFeatureTokenizer with a Periodic Non-Linear Embedding Tokenizer and upgrade the output head from single [CLS] extraction to attentive multi-token pooling with a residual input feature skip connection. WHY: Tabular expenditures and age exhibit multimodal distributions and heavy zero-inflation that 1D linear projections cannot separate, while single [CLS] readouts create an information bottleneck that attenuates gradient flow across 30+ tabular tokens. HOW: Implement periodic encoding mapping continuous scalars through learned frequencies into sine and cosine bases followed by linear projection to d_token, and update TabularGCAN's readout to compute an attention-weighted sum of contextualized tokens fused with pooled input embeddings before passing to the classification MLP. Interface constraints: Preserve class signature TabularGCAN(num_continuous, cat_cardinalities, ...) and forward(x_num, x_cat) returning 1D binary classification logits."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The baseline model plateaued at 81.35% validation accuracy with high inter-fold variance due to representation bottlenecks: 1D scalar linear tokenization cannot capture zero-inflated luxury expenditure thresholds, discrete boolean predictors such as CryoSleep are diluted by standard scaling, and a single [CLS] token readout bottleneck discards feature activations. Focusing on data_processing_and_feature_engineering and model_design directly resolves these root causes by cleanly isolating discrete switches into categorical embeddings and replacing linear projections with periodic non-linear tokenizers and attentive residual pooling.",
  "module": [
