  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Reclassify binary indicators (CryoSleep, VIP, HasSpent, IsSolo, IsSoloFamily, IsInfant, IsChild, IsTeen, IsSenior) and discrete spatial indicators (CabinRegion) from numerical continuous features into categorical features. WHY: CryoSleep is the most decisive predictor in the dataset, and boolean states represent discrete qualitative regimes; standardizing them as continuous floats forces an arbitrary linear scale, whereas categorical assignment allows the model to learn unconstrained distinct embeddings. HOW: In process_features(), append these discrete columns to categorical_cols, ensure non-negative integer encoding without deprecated downcasting warnings, and leave strictly continuous features in numerical_cols. Interface constraints: Retain the function signature process_features() returning (train_processed, test_processed, categorical_cols, numerical_cols) and maintain consistent column names.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the 1D linear NumericalFeatureTokenizer with a Periodic Non-Linear Embedding Tokenizer and upgrade the output head from single [CLS] extraction to attentive multi-token pooling with a residual input feature skip connection. WHY: Tabular expenditures and age exhibit multimodal distributions and heavy zero-inflation that 1D linear projections cannot separate, while single [CLS] readouts create an information bottleneck that attenuates gradient flow across 30+ tabular tokens. HOW: Implement periodic encoding mapping continuous scalars through learned frequencies into sine and cosine bases followed by linear projection to d_token, and update TabularGCAN's readout to compute an attention-weighted sum of contextualized tokens fused with pooled input embeddings before passing to the classification MLP. Interface constraints: Preserve class signature TabularGCAN(num_continuous, cat_cardinalities, ...) and forward(x_num, x_cat) returning 1D binary classification logits."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "The TabularResNet model currently exhibits early overfitting (train loss 0.3234 vs. validation loss 0.4512, plateauing at 0.7867 accuracy) because extreme right-tailed continuous spending features distort neural representations, spatial Deck-Side interactions and group-level contexts are missing, and training on only a single fold discards 20% of training samples while inflating validation variance. Focusing on data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses the complete end-to-end bottleneck by normalizing continuous distributions, equipping the architecture with adaptive Squeeze-and-Excitation feature recalibration, and leveraging full 5-fold ensembling for maximum generalization.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Fit a scikit-learn QuantileTransformer with a Gaussian output distribution on training continuous features, engineer spatial interaction tokens ('Deck_Side' combining CabinDeck and CabinSide), and create group-level context aggregations (group mean total spending and group cryosleep ratio). WHY: Raw and log-transformed amenity expenditures still exhibit severe zero-inflation and extreme heavy right tails that distort linear layers, while physical ship location and party-level behavior are strong determinants of dimensional transport. HOW: In engineer_features(), generate 'Deck_Side' by concatenating CabinDeck and CabinSide and compute group aggregates via groupby('GroupID') without target leakage; in prepare_datasets(), fit QuantileTransformer(output_distribution='normal', random_state=42) strictly on training numerical features and transform validation and test sets. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve engineer_features() and prepare_datasets() outputs and ensure all engineered continuous, binary, and categorical feature names remain registered in metadata.json.", "model_design": "WHAT: Integrate a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) feature recalibration block into TabularResNet directly following feature fusion and input normalization. WHY: The existing TabularResNet directly projects and fuses continuous and categorical features without channel-wise dependency weighting, preventing the network from adaptively suppressing spending features when categorical states indicate CryoSleep. HOW: Implement an SEBlock module using a two-layer bottleneck MLP with GELU and Sigmoid gating that rescales fused feature channels by learned attention weights prior to passing them through the residual GLU blocks. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain the TabularResNet constructor signature and forward(x_num, x_cat) -> logits interface to ensure full compatibility with the existing loss function and data loaders.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Upgrade the training and evaluation loop from a single-fold run to a full 5-fold Stratified Group Cross-Validation pipeline with out-of-fold validation scoring and 5-fold test ensembling. WHY: Evaluating only fold 0 discards 20% of training data during inference, suffers from split-specific variance, and prevents full exploitation of the ~8700 training passengers within the 20-minute execution budget. HOW: In main(), iterate through folds 0 to 4 using the predefined StratifiedGroupKFold splits, train a model on each fold with early stopping and CosineAnnealingLR, collect out-of-fold probability predictions to compute the audited global out-of-fold accuracy, and average test probabilities across all 5 models to write final predictions to ./submission/submission.csv. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain the metric print format 'Final Validation Score: <score>' based on total out-of-fold classification accuracy, and format submission.csv strictly with 'PassengerId' and boolean 'Transported'."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The TabularResNet model currently exhibits early overfitting (train loss 0.3234 vs. validation loss 0.4512, plateauing at 0.7867 accuracy) because extreme right-tailed continuous spending features distort neural representations, spatial Deck-Side interactions and group-level contexts are missing, and training on only a single fold discards 20% of training samples while inflating validation variance. Focusing on data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses the complete end-to-end bottleneck by normalizing continuous distributions, equipping the architecture with adaptive Squeeze-and-Excitation feature recalibration, and leveraging full 5-fold ensembling for maximum generalization.",
