    "model_design": "WHAT: Integrate a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) feature recalibration block into TabularResNet directly following feature fusion and input normalization. WHY: The existing TabularResNet directly projects and fuses continuous and categorical features without channel-wise dependency weighting, preventing the network from adaptively suppressing spending features when categorical states indicate CryoSleep. HOW: Implement an SEBlock module using a two-layer bottleneck MLP with GELU and Sigmoid gating that rescales fused feature channels by learned attention weights prior to passing them through the residual GLU blocks. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain the TabularResNet constructor signature and forward(x_num, x_cat) -> logits interface to ensure full compatibility with the existing loss function and data loaders.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Upgrade the training and evaluation loop from a single-fold run to a full 5-fold Stratified Group Cross-Validation pipeline with out-of-fold validation scoring and 5-fold test ensembling. WHY: Evaluating only fold 0 discards 20% of training data during inference, suffers from split-specific variance, and prevents full exploitation of the ~8700 training passengers within the 20-minute execution budget. HOW: In main(), iterate through folds 0 to 4 using the predefined StratifiedGroupKFold splits, train a model on each fold with early stopping and CosineAnnealingLR, collect out-of-fold probability predictions to compute the audited global out-of-fold accuracy, and average test probabilities across all 5 models to write final predictions to ./submission/submission.csv. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain the metric print format 'Final Validation Score: <score>' based on total out-of-fold classification accuracy, and format submission.csv strictly with 'PassengerId' and boolean 'Transported'."
