}"}

{"reason": "TabularGCAN suffers from acute overfitting where training loss collapses to 0.27 while validation loss explodes above 0.52 and truncates validation accuracy at 0.8061. The root cause is a combination of silent data corruption in data processing—where unspent passengers with missing CryoSleep were incorrectly forced to False (awake)—and unregularized attention memorization paired with hard binary cross-entropy overconfidence in model design. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering and model_design directly resolves these bottlenecks through clean ternary CryoSleep encoding, localized spatial cabin binning, feature token dropout, wide-residual skip routing, and label-smoothed binary cross-entropy.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "1) WHAT: Implement an explicit ternary categorical representation for CryoSleep (0 = Awake, 1 = Asleep, 2 = Unknown/Missing) with a dedicated missingness indicator, and engineer localized spatial cabin cluster bins (grouping CabinNum into 50-cabin windows intersected with Deck and Side). 2) WHY: The current pipeline erroneously mapped NaN CryoSleep records with zero spend to False (awake), corrupting the single most predictive feature in the competition, while continuous cabin numbers fail to capture localized hull breach damage patterns. 3) HOW: In process_features(), retain NaN CryoSleep after physical spend deductions, encode it explicitly into 3 categorical states (0, 1, 2) alongside a boolean CryoSleep_is_na indicator, compute CabinCluster50 as (CabinNum // 50).astype(int), interact it into CabinDeck_Side_Cluster, and register them into categorical_cols. 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve the process_features() return signature returning (train_processed, test_processed, categorical_cols, numerical_cols) and maintain metadata export to ./working/feature_metadata.json.", "model_design": "1) WHAT: Introduce Feature Token Dropout (stochastic token masking at rate 0.10) prior to transformer blocks, a parallel Wide-Residual shortcut connecting pooled input tokens directly to the classification head, and a Label-Smoothed Binary Cross-Entropy loss criterion (epsilon = 0.05). 2) WHY: Deep self-attention overfits to feature co-dependencies without stochastic token regularization, raw first-order signals are attenuated without a direct wide residual pathway, and unregularized BCE encourages extreme logit overconfidence on noisy tabular labels. 3) HOW: In TabularGCAN, apply a dropout mask over token vectors along the sequence dimension during training, compute an attentive or mean-pooled representation of the initial tokens to bypass the transformer stack directly into the head MLP, and implement LabelSmoothedBCEWithLogitsLoss within get_loss_criterion(eps=0.05). 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Retain class signatures for TabularGCAN(num_continuous, cat_cardinalities, ...) and its forward(x_num, x_cat) returning 1D logits, and maintain get_loss_criterion() returning an nn.Module compatible with the existing training loop."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "TabularGCAN suffers from acute overfitting where training loss collapses to 0.27 while validation loss explodes above 0.52 and truncates validation accuracy at 0.8061. The root cause is a combination of silent data corruption in data processing—where unspent passengers with missing CryoSleep were incorrectly forced to False (awake)—and unregularized attention memorization paired with hard binary cross-entropy overconfidence in model design. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering and model_design directly resolves these bottlenecks through clean ternary CryoSleep encoding, localized spatial cabin binning, feature token dropout, wide-residual skip routing, and label-smoothed binary cross-entropy.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "1) WHAT: Implement an explicit ternary categorical representation for CryoSleep (0 = Awake, 1 = Asleep, 2 = Unknown/Missing) with a dedicated missingness indicator, and engineer localized spatial cabin cluster bins (grouping CabinNum into 50-cabin windows intersected with Deck and Side). 2) WHY: The current pipeline erroneously mapped NaN CryoSleep records with zero spend to False (awake), corrupting the single most predictive feature in the competition, while continuous cabin numbers fail to capture localized hull breach damage patterns. 3) HOW: In process_features(), retain NaN CryoSleep after physical spend deductions, encode it explicitly into 3 categorical states (0, 1, 2) alongside a boolean CryoSleep_is_na indicator, compute CabinCluster50 as (CabinNum // 50).astype(int), interact it into CabinDeck_Side_Cluster, and register them into categorical_cols. 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve the process_features() return signature returning (train_processed, test_processed, categorical_cols, numerical_cols) and maintain metadata export to ./working/feature_metadata.json.",
    "model_design": "1) WHAT: Introduce Feature Token Dropout (stochastic token masking at rate 0.10) prior to transformer blocks, a parallel Wide-Residual shortcut connecting pooled input tokens directly to the classification head, and a Label-Smoothed Binary Cross-Entropy loss criterion (epsilon = 0.05). 2) WHY: Deep self-attention overfits to feature co-dependencies without stochastic token regularization, raw first-order signals are attenuated without a direct wide residual pathway, and unregularized BCE encourages extreme logit overconfidence on noisy tabular labels. 3) HOW: In TabularGCAN, apply a dropout mask over token vectors along the sequence dimension during training, compute an attentive or mean-pooled representation of the initial tokens to bypass the transformer stack directly into the head MLP, and implement LabelSmoothedBCEWithLogitsLoss within get_loss_criterion(eps=0.05). 4) INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Retain class signatures for TabularGCAN(num_continuous, cat_cardinalities, ...) and its forward(x_num, x_cat) returning 1D logits, and maintain get_loss_criterion() returning an nn.Module compatible with the existing training loop."
  }
}"}

{"reason": "Execution results show severe divergence between training loss (dropping to 0.3203) and validation loss (climbing to 0.4997) across all folds, caused by monolithic input projections that discard localized pairwise feature identities and residual blocks that lack feature-level regularization. Modifying model_design and training_evaluation provides the most targeted solution: it replaces global linear projections with a per-feature Tokenizer and Multi-Head Self-Attention to capture sparse conditional dependencies (e.g., CryoSleep strictly gating luxury expenditures) while applying Feature Token Dropout and Stochastic Depth to prevent over-parameterization on ~6,900 fold samples.", "module": ["model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"model_design": "WHAT: Replace the monolithic linear projections with a per-feature Tokenizer projecting each numerical and categorical feature into a shared embedding space (d=32), append a Multi-Head Feature Self-Attention (MHSA) interaction layer, and add Stochastic Depth (DropPath rate 0.10) to the TabularResNet residual blocks. WHY: Spaceship Titanic features possess strong inter-feature constraints (such as CryoSleep governing amenity expenditures and HomePlanet constraining deck assignments) that are obliterated when columns are flattened into two monolithic vectors before interaction. HOW: Implement a tokenizer that maps each continuous feature via an individual linear transformation and each categorical feature via an embedding layer into 32 dimensions, apply an nn.MultiheadAttention(embed_dim=32, num_heads=4, batch_first=True) layer with residual connection and LayerNorm, flatten or project the recalibrated tokens into hidden_dim, and integrate DropPath into TabularResNetBlock residual pathways. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Retain the TabularResNet constructor signature and preserve forward(x_num, x_cat) returning 1D binary logits of shape (batch, 1).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Implement Feature Token Dropout (rate 0.10) during the training forward pass and increase AdamW weight decay from 1e-4 to 1e-3. WHY: Fold training trajectories demonstrate severe overfitting where validation loss rebounds as early as epoch 6 while training loss continues plunging, indicating brittle co-adaptation on dominant feature signals. HOW: In TabularResNet during training mode, randomly mask out 10% of the token vectors along the token sequence dimension using Bernoulli masking, and configure AdamW in main() with weight_decay=1e-3 alongside the existing CosineAnnealingLR scheduler. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain the 5-fold StratifiedGroupKFold loop grouped on GroupID, retain the metric output string 'Final Validation Score: <score>', and preserve submission generation at ./submission/submission.csv with PassengerId and boolean Transported columns."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
